# Agent Team Control Plane

This chart is the canonical compact view of the evolving agent-team development loop. It complements the detailed SSOTs and skills rather than replacing them.

## Evidence contract

A node transition is not proof of success. Promotion requires attributable evidence. In particular, an HTTP success, workflow success, review acknowledgement, low latency, or large response is not by itself a successful task outcome.

The telemetry lineage is:

`SHA → workflow run → job → step → logs/artifacts → outcome → review → promotion decision`.

## Team population

Scout discovers provider/model candidates. Manager/MoneyBall/3L0 scores them using observed evidence. OX-Alpha, DeepSeek, Gemini and future providers are population members, not permanent hardcoded winners.

## BIUDL

BIUDL means broad integration → focused development lane → thin validated slice → feed-forward synthesis → broaden. A successful thin slice is promoted only with evidence and then becomes reusable team knowledge.

